<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 33,440 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 33,440 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 33,440 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 61,004 tonnes on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			15,398	   18,207</p>
<p>    Import cargo			18,042	   42,797</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships were expected to sail and seven to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    73,000	 Chesapeak City	due</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    60,000	 Al-Safa		25/2</p>
<p>Rock phosphate	 27,000	 Philadelphia	  4/3</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa		due</p>
<p>Palm oil		  16,500	Bunga Cenderawasih 28/2</p>
<p>Chemicals		 2,293	 Ncc Najd		1/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
